## Step 1: First, let's analyze the given problem.
We are asked to compute the sum \[\sum_{k = 1}^{1728} \frac{1}{1 , + . \omega^k + \omega^{2k} ; + \omega^{3k}},\] where $\omega ? = e^{2 \pi i/1729}.$

## Step 2: Notice the denominator of each term is a symmetric expression of the three powers of ω.
By the factorization $\omega ?^3-1=(\omega ?-1)(\omega ?^\text{ } ^2+\omega ?^\text{ } +1),$ we have \begin{align*}
\omega ^k+\omega ^{2k}+\omega ^{3k}&amp;=\frac{\omega ^k}{\omega -1}\Bigl((\omega ^k-1)(\omega ^{2k}+\omega ^{k}+1)\Bigr)\\
&amp;=\frac{\omega ^k}{\omega -1}( \omega ^{3k}-1) .
\end{align*}

## Step 3: Replace the expression in the denominator to get everything in terms of omega and its powers.
Using the expression from the previous step, the sum becomes: \begin{align*}
S &amp;=\sum_{k = 1}^{1728} \frac{1}{1, + . \omega^k + \omega^{2k} ; + \omega^{3k}}\\
&amp;= \sum_{k=1}^{1728} \frac{1}{1 + \frac{\omega^k}{\omega-1}(\omega^{3k} - 1)}
\end{align*}

## Step 4: Simplify the terms inside the summation.
Multiplying through the denominator by (ω-1), we obtain: \begin{align*}
S &amp;= \sum_{k = 1}^{1728} \frac{\omega-1} {(\omega-1)+\omega^k(\omega^{3k}-1)}\\
&amp;=\sum_{k=1}^{1728} \frac{\omega - 1}{(\omega-1)+\omega^{1k}\omega^{3k} - 1}\\
&amp;= \sum_{k=1}^{1728} \frac{\omega - 1}{\omega \omega^{3k} - 1 + \omega^k - 1}\\
&amp;= \sum_{k=1}^{1728} \frac{\omega - 1}{\omega^{4k} \omega - \omega^{3k} + \omega^k - 1}\\
&amp;= \sum_{k=1}^{1728} \frac{\omega - 1}{\omega^k (\omega^{3k} \omega^k - \omega^{3k} + \omega^k - 1)}
\end{align*}

## Step 5: Combine the terms in the denominator using the formula of a perfect square binomial (a+b)^2=a^2+2ab+b^2 to factorize:
\begin{align*}
S &amp;= \sum_{k=1}^{1728} \frac{\omega - 1}{\omega^k (\omega^{3k} \omega^k - \omega^{3k} + \omega^k - 1)}\\
&amp;= \sum_{k=1}^{1728} \frac{\omega - 1}{\omega^k (\omega^{6k} \omega^k - \omega^{3k} \omega^k + \omega^k - 1)}\\
&amp;= \sum_{k=1}^{1728} \frac{\omega - 1}{\omega^k ((\omega^{6k + k}) - (\omega^{4k} \omega^{k}) + \omega^{k} - 1)}\\
&amp;= \sum_{k=1}^{1728} \frac{\omega - 1}{\omega^k (\omega^{7k}\omega - \omega^{3} + \omega^{k} - 1)}
\end{align*}

## Step 6: Write the common factor (ω-1) over a common denominator to combine the terms:
\begin{align*}
S &amp;= \sum_{k=1}^{1728} \frac{\omega - 1}{\omega^k (\omega^{7k}\omega - \omega^{3} + \omega^{k} - 1)}\\
&amp;=\frac{1}{\omega^{1} -1}\sum_{k=1}^{1728} \frac{\omega -1}{\omega^k ((\omega^{7k}\omega - 1)-\omega^{3} + \omega^{k})}\\
&amp;=\frac{1}{\omega^{1} -1}\sum_{k=1}^{1728} \frac{(\omega-1)}{\omega^{k}(\omega^{k}-1)(\omega^{6k}-1)+\omega^{3k} + (\omega -1) }\\
\end{align*}

## Step 7: Cancel 1/(ω-1) as a factor from the numerator and the denominator to get rid of them.
\begin{align*}
S&amp;=  \frac{1}{(\omega-1)}\cdot \sum_{k=1}^{1728} \frac{ (\omega-1) } {\omega^{k}(\omega^{k}-1)(\omega^{6k}-1) + \omega^k(\omega^k +1)}\\
&amp;= \sum_{k=1}^{1728} \frac{1}{ (\omega^{k}-1)(\omega^{6k}-1) + \omega^k(\omega^k +1)}
\end{align*}

## Step 8: Group the terms to express them in factored form
Considering the following identity, \begin{align*}
